Subtask 3.2: Introduce and Monitor Errors
Create a destination rule to introduce some errors:
cat > fault-injection.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: VirtualService
metadata:
  name: reviews-fault
spec:
  hosts:
  - reviews
  http:
  - fault:
      abort:
        percentage:
          value: 20
        httpStatus: 500
    route:
    - destination:
        host: reviews
EOF
Apply the fault injection:
kubectl apply -f fault-injection.yaml
Wait 2-3 minutes for traffic to accumulate, then observe in Kiali:

Red edges indicate errors in communication
Error percentages are displayed on the edges
Failed requests are shown in red in the graph
Click on the red edge between productpage and reviews to see:

Error rate percentage
HTTP status code distribution
Success vs. failure metrics
