Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Kiali Dashboard Not Accessible
Problem: Cannot access Kiali at localhost:20001

Solution:

# Check if port-forward is running
ps aux | grep kubectl

# Restart port-forward if needed
kubectl port-forward svc/kiali -n istio-system 20001:20001
Issue 2: No Traffic Visible in Graph
Problem: Graph shows services but no traffic

Solutions:

Ensure traffic generation script is running:
ps aux | grep generate-traffic
Check if services have Istio sidecars:
kubectl get pods -o wide
Verify time range is appropriate (try "Last 1 hour")
Issue 3: Services Not Showing in Graph
Problem: Expected services don't appear in the graph

Solution:

# Check namespace selection in Kiali
# Verify pods are running with sidecars
kubectl describe pod <pod-name>

# Check Istio injection
kubectl get namespace -L istio-injection
Cleanup
Stop the traffic generation script:
pkill -f generate-traffic
Remove the fault injection:
kubectl delete -f fault-injection.yaml
Optionally, remove the sample application:
kubectl delete -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/istio/istio/release-1.20/samples/bookinfo/platform/kube/bookinfo.yaml
kubectl delete -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/istio/istio/release-1.20/samples/bookinfo/networking/bookinfo-gateway.yaml
